18. Core Proposition

Safe & Sane therefore proposes a shift from:

“How do we document and prevent every possible failure?”

toward:

“How do we continuously maintain a system’s correspondence with reality, while its entities exercise responsible judgment, respond to observed change, reduce preventable risk, remain resilient to unforeseeable conditions, and continuously update the configuration?”

This does not replace rules, standards, policies, technical controls, risk methodologies, safety engineering, cybersecurity, AI evaluation, or human oversight.

It provides a proposed governing architecture within which those mechanisms can participate.

The central research question remains empirical:

Does this configuration-centric, continuously reconciled architecture provide a useful and demonstrable improvement in identifying, understanding, preventing, containing, or recovering from harmful system trajectories?

Safe & Sane itself remains subject to the same test.
